{"id": "67b5fac2-d5e5-47f0-8d2f-29b8e4c3a5ee", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "By default, knowledge bases are encrypted with an AWS-owned key, and the serverSideEncryptionConfiguration field only shows up for fully managed knowledge bases with a KMS key set at creation. For a VECTOR KB backed by OpenSearch Serverless, that field is typically absent since encryption at rest is instead governed by the OSS collection's own encryption policy, which is always active using either an AWS-owned key or a CMK.

So the absence of this field shouldn't be flagged as "unencrypted" -- the right call is compliant/pass if default AWS-owned encryption is acceptable, or at most a note that CMK usage can't be confirmed from this field alone and would require checking the OSS collection's encryption policy separately.

"}]}
